>interesting game.
 ^^^^^^^^^^^
 I can easily believe you! I'd like to see that kind of game, but I don't
 want to see anymore 2 different versions of nethack around. Did someone of
 the dev team play to your game?

>Since everyone always talks about what should be added:

>		Top Five Things To Drop From Nethack

>	5. Treasure vaults.  (Boring and mostly ignored.)

	This must be kept in the game. $$ are useful to get intrinsics from
	a priest, and you can force a vault to get them...

>	4. Sinks. (A one-shot joke that adds little.)

	I rarely use them, but I'm not a great player. I know they are useful
	to identify rings, to get polyformed, and to do other things (read
	the SPOILER file :-)

>	3. All anachronisms. (Camera, credit card, ice chest, Hawaian shirt...)

	Ok for camera, credit card, ice chest, and maybe K and C rations...
	But please save the Hawaian shirt! Just rename it...

>	2. Boulders,statues and gems. (Boulders are an annoyance, statues
>	       	are stupid [are there sculptors running around the dungeon?],
>		and gems are only useful to anal types who are trying to
>		max out the score file.)

	Boulders are useful! You can use them to fill the moat of the castle
	and you can broke them with a pick-axe to get rocks to kill a nymph
	keeping your distance.

>	1. Rust monsters. (Just 'cause I hate these.)
	
	They're not so terrible...

